{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011vtP86podnAHMP4kmjpSt3","type":"tool_result","content":"6023:E.tex = {\n6045:  dirt(x, y, o = {}) {\n6069:// the floor textures as materials: floorMat: 'dirt' draws E.tex.dirt, and the same names work on every other surface\n6073:  dirt: { color: '#9a7048', pattern: 'speck', floor: (x, y) => E.tex.dirt(x, y) },\n1:# Objects and materials as data\n3:The full engine draws still objects (barrels, tables, trees, wells) from a few lines of data, in every view and facing,\n9:## Use one\n13:r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing: Math.PI / 2 });\n34:## The core library\n36:**Shapes** (sized for a 26-unit hero; generators take params): barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed,\n39:`r.shape('pine', x, y, 0, { params: { h: 30 } })`; `E.SHAPES.barrel.about` says what each is.\n46:## Materials on surfaces\n84:## Write one\n116:### Worked entries\n119:barrel: { about: 'oak barrel, two iron hoops', tags: 'container wood', mats: { w: 'oak', h: 'iron' },\n135:## Make one: the recipe\n145:   alone works too: `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs barrel`). It draws `check-output/asset-sheet/stool.png`: every view and\n155:## Limits","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8704baa7-6f68-414d-afec-f55fd2d8121c","uuid":"b6d92057-44bd-4d6d-b8ca-c80f8d01634e","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:41:17.394Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"6023:E.tex = {\n6045:  dirt(x, y, o = {}) {\n6069:// the floor textures as materials: floorMat: 'dirt' draws E.tex.dirt, and the same names work on every other surface\n6073:  dirt: { color: '#9a7048', pattern: 'speck', floor: (x, y) => E.tex.dirt(x, y) },\n1:# Objects and materials as data\n3:The full engine draws still objects (barrels, tables, trees, wells) from a few lines of data, in every view and facing,\n9:## Use one\n13:r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing: Math.PI / 2 });\n34:## The core library\n36:**Shapes** (sized for a 26-unit hero; generators take params): barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed,\n39:`r.shape('pine', x, y, 0, { params: { h: 30 } })`; `E.SHAPES.barrel.about` says what each is.\n46:## Materials on surfaces\n84:## Write one\n116:### Worked entries\n119:barrel: { about: 'oak barrel, two iron hoops', tags: 'container wood', mats: { w: 'oak', h: 'iron' },\n135:## Make one: the recipe\n145:   alone works too: `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs barrel`). It draws `check-output/asset-sheet/stool.png`: every view and\n155:## Limits","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011vtP86podnAHMP4kmjpSt3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf9JLyvsSGiyNp3BtHga","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y3CrCyNn8YYjUyjGVXPFNf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-183711__xb81546/work/Walter*/vendor/engine\nsed -n 34,84p docs-ASSETS.md | cut -c1-700; sed -n 6023,6068p my-3d2dge.js | cut -c1-200; node -e \"\nconst vm=require('vm');const fs=require('fs');const c={console};vm.createContext(c);vm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync('my-3d2dge.js','utf8'),c);console.log(Object.keys(c.My3D2dge.SHAPES).join(' '));console.log(Object.keys(c.My3D2dge.MATERIALS).join(' '))\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5135,"cache_read_input_tokens":115059,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5135,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8704baa7-6f68-414d-afec-f55fd2d8121c","uuid":"0a9d04b5-bb81-4b45-aa2b-e302a5c2bc90","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:41:20.730Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf9JLdrLvJQt8FPSHjoh","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Y3CrCyNn8YYjUyjGVXPFNf":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-183711__xb81546/work/Walter*/vendor/engine\nsed -n 34,84p docs-ASSETS.md | cut -c1-700; sed -n 6023,6068p my-3d2dge.js | cut -c1-200; node -e \"\nconst vm=require('vm');const fs=require('fs');const c={console};vm.createContext(c);vm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync('my-3d2dge.js','utf8'),c);console.log(Object.keys(c.My3D2dge.SHAPES).join(' '));console.log(Object.keys(c.My3D2dge.MATERIALS).join(' '))\""}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y3CrCyNn8YYjUyjGVXPFNf","type":"tool_result","content":"## The core library\n\n**Shapes** (sized for a 26-unit hero; generators take params): barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed,\nbookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, well, sign, lamppost, anvil; fence { len: 16 }, pine { h: 41, tiers: 4 },\ntree { h: 40, seed: 1 }, bush { r: 7 }, grass { h: 6, n: 6 }, rock { r: 7.5, seed: 2 }, crystal { h: 18, seed: 1 }.\n`r.shape('pine', x, y, 0, { params: { h: 30 } })`; `E.SHAPES.barrel.about` says what each is.\n\n**Materials:** woods oak walnut birch crate plank planks wood; stones stone cobble marble granite sandstone slate rock\nbrick flagstone ruin; metals iron steel gold copper bronze metal rusted; clay glazed porcelain; cloth linen burlap wool velvet leather;\nplants bark needles leaves shrub moss straw hedge grass; ground dirt sand snow mud; water ice crystal flame bone shingle;\nwalls timber plaster; tops speckle plain tiles slab; tiles block bonus ground pipe checker.\n\n## Materials on surfaces\n\n```js\nE.MATERIALS.mossy = { color: '#6a7a5a', pattern: 'stones', size: 6 };   // or the shorthand '#6a7a5a stones size=6'\nconst types = { 1: { h: 32, top: '#6a6280', side: '#4a4360', face: 'cobble', roof: 'slate' } };   // TileMap walls\nconst map = new E.TileMap({ rows, legend, types, floorMat: 'flagstone', floorMats: { water: 'water' } });   // floors\nconst level = new E.PlatformMap({ rows, legend, types: { 1: { kind: 'solid', style: 'block', mat: 'mossy' } } });\n```\n\nfloorMats is keyed by the floor tags of the legend ('~': { floor: 'water' }); either stands in for floorTex.\n\nA material is `{ color, pattern, ...the pattern's numbers, ramp, glow, over }`. Its five tones come from `E.tones(color)`\n(or its own `ramp` of five, dark to light); the light picks a band, the pattern moves it a step, so a material works on\nevery surface and in every palette and recolors with one hex. An unknown name warns with the list of names.\nOverlays, the last on top, each in its own color's tones: `over: [['moss', '#5f7a3a', { up: .6 }], ['cracks']]`; moss on\nwhat looks up, cracks (the material a step darker), dirt near the ground (h 6), rust; each takes amount and size.\n\n| Pattern | Numbers | What |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| none | | the light alone |\n| planks | bw 3, len 14, dir | boards with joints; staves on round parts; dir: 'v' turns them |\n| crate | frame 2, bw 3 | a framed, braced side; planks on its lid |\n| bricks | bw 6, bh 3, mortar | running bond |\n| stones | size 5 | irregular stones (Voronoi), dark joints, a lit rim |\n| tiles | size 4 | square tiles, grout |\n| speck, noise | amount .08; scale 4 | specks; soft patches |\n| foliage | size 3.5 | leaf clumps lit on top |\n| bark | | fissures; rings on a cut end |\n| metal | rivet | a shine where lit; rivets |\n| cloth | fold .9 | weave and folds |\n| glaze | | a glossy shine |\n| thatch, shingles | course; bw | straw courses; roof tiles |\n\nYour own pattern: `E.PATTERNS.waves = (s, m) => Math.sin(s.u / (m.size || 3)) > .8 ? 1 : 0` (s.u, s.v: world units\nacross and up the surface; s.lid, s.curved, s.lit, s.W, s.H; return a step, -1 to +2). A material may also paint one kind\nof surface its own way, per pixel: `face(wx, z, tones, type, cx, cy, fi, nh, h)` or `roof(wx, wy, tones, type)` returning\na color or null, `floor(x, y, tag, view)` returning [r, g, b].\n\n## Write one\nE.tex = {\n  /** stone flagstones with running-bond rows. pal: {stones:[hex..], mortar, hi, lo, speck} */\n  flagstone(x, y, pal, size = 16) {\n    const row = Math.floor(y / size), off = (row & 1) * size / 2, col = Math.floor((x + off) / size), lx = x + off - col * size, ly = y - row * size;\n    if (lx < 1 || ly < 1) return pal.mortar;\n    const h = hash2(col, row); let c = pal.stones[(h * pal.stones.length) | 0];\n    if (lx < 2 || ly < 2) c = pal.hi; else if (lx > size - 1.5 || ly > size - 1.5) c = pal.lo;\n    const n = hash2(Math.floor(x * 1.3), Math.floor(y * 1.3)); if (n < .05) c = pal.speck;\n    if (h > .93 && lx > 3 && lx < size - 3 && Math.abs(lx - ly * .7 - 3) < .6) c = pal.mortar;\n    return c;\n  },\n  /** grass with darker tufts and a few flowers. o: { base, dark, light, flower } hex colors */\n  grass(x, y, o = {}) {\n    // blotches of light and dark grass at two scales, short blade marks, rare flower clusters (no single-pixel static)\n    const n = noise2(x * .07, y * .07) * .65 + noise2(x * .23, y * .23) * .35, blade = noise2(x * .9, y * .35);\n    const fl = noise2(x * .12 + 40, y * .12 + 40), fh = hash2(Math.floor(x / 2), Math.floor(y / 2));\n    if (fl > .82 && fh > .8) return hex(fh > .93 ? (o.flower || '#f4e27a') : (o.flower2 || '#f2f2f6'));\n    if (n > .66 || (blade > .78 && n > .5)) return hex(o.dark || '#3e8a3a');\n    if (n < .34 || blade < .16) return hex(o.light || '#6cc25a');\n    return hex(o.base || '#55a94a');\n  },\n  /** dirt, sand or snow: base color with soft noise and specks. o: { base, dark, light } */\n  dirt(x, y, o = {}) {\n    // soft patches plus small pebbles (2-3 px clusters with a lit edge), no static\n    const n = noise2(x * .1, y * .1) * .7 + noise2(x * .3, y * .3) * .3, peb = noise2(x * .45 + 9, y * .45 + 3);\n    if (peb > .84) return hex(noise2(x * .45 + 9, (y - 1) * .45 + 3) > .84 ? (o.dark || '#6e4a2e') : (o.light || '#c9a276'));\n    return hex(n > .62 ? (o.light || '#b08a5e') : n < .3 ? (o.dark || '#7d5838') : (o.base || '#9a7048'));\n  },\n  /** water with static ripple lines (baked, so it does not move). o: { base, dark, light } */\n  water(x, y, o = {}) {\n    const w = Math.sin(x * .35 + Math.sin(y * .18) * 2.2 + y * .05);\n    if (w > .93 && ((Math.floor(x) + Math.floor(y)) & 1)) return hex(o.light || '#9fe3ff');\n    return hex(noise2(x * .05, y * .05) > .55 ? (o.base || '#2f7fd0') : (o.dark || '#2464b0'));\n  },\n  /** wooden floor boards running along x. o: { base, dark, line } */\n  planks(x, y, o = {}) {\n    const row = Math.floor(y / 6), ly = y - row * 6, len = 20 + Math.floor(hash2(row, 3) * 18), joint = (x + row * 13) % len;\n    if (ly < 1 || joint < 1) return hex(o.line || '#4a2e1c');\n    const g = hash2(Math.floor(x / 3), row); return hex(g > .7 ? (o.dark || '#8a5a34') : (o.base || '#9d6a3f'));\n  },\n  /** checkerboard tiles (castle floors, bonus rooms). o: { a, b, size } */\n  checker(x, y, o = {}) { const s = o.size || 16; return hex(((Math.floor(x / s) + Math.floor(y / s)) & 1) ? (o.a || '#d8d0e8') : (o.b || '#5a5270')); },\n  /** plain color with light noise, for roads, carpets and space floors. o: { base, amount } */\n  plain(x, y, o = {}) { const c = hex(o.base || '#4a4458'), k = 1 + (Math.round((noise2(x * .15, y * .15) - .5) * 4) / 4) * (o.amount === undefined ? .14 : o.amount); return c.map(v => v * k); }\n};\n\nbarrel crate chest table chair stool bench bed bookcase shelf pot jar sack cart well sign lamppost anvil fence pine tree bush grass rock crystal\nbrick stone rock plank timber plaster hedge speckle plain tiles slab leaves grass flagstone dirt water planks checker wood metal ground pipe block bonus oak walnut birch crate cobble marble granite sandstone slate iron steel gold copper bronze clay glazed porcelain linen burlap wool velvet leather bark needles shrub moss straw sand snow mud shingle bone ice crystal flame ruin rusted","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8704baa7-6f68-414d-afec-f55fd2d8121c","uuid":"ab5589f0-846f-4692-b61d-ddbe82bdab74","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:41:20.793Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## The core library\n\n**Shapes** (sized for a 26-unit hero; generators take params): barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed,\nbookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, well, sign, lamppost, anvil; fence { len: 16 }, pine { h: 41, tiers: 4 },\ntree { h: 40, seed: 1 }, bush { r: 7 }, grass { h: 6, n: 6 }, rock { r: 7.5, seed: 2 }, crystal { h: 18, seed: 1 }.\n`r.shape('pine', x, y, 0, { params: { h: 30 } })`; `E.SHAPES.barrel.about` says what each is.\n\n**Materials:** woods oak walnut birch crate plank planks wood; stones stone cobble marble granite sandstone slate rock\nbrick flagstone ruin; metals iron steel gold copper bronze metal rusted; clay glazed porcelain; cloth linen burlap wool velvet leather;\nplants bark needles leaves shrub moss straw hedge grass; ground dirt sand snow mud; water ice crystal flame bone shingle;\nwalls timber plaster; tops speckle plain tiles slab; tiles block bonus ground pipe checker.\n\n## Materials on surfaces\n\n```js\nE.MATERIALS.mossy = { color: '#6a7a5a', pattern: 'stones', size: 6 };   // or the shorthand '#6a7a5a stones size=6'\nconst types = { 1: { h: 32, top: '#6a6280', side: '#4a4360', face: 'cobble', roof: 'slate' } };   // TileMap walls\nconst map = new E.TileMap({ rows, legend, types, floorMat: 'flagstone', floorMats: { water: 'water' } });   // floors\nconst level = new E.PlatformMap({ rows, legend, types: { 1: { kind: 'solid', style: 'block', mat: 'mossy' } } });\n```\n\nfloorMats is keyed by the floor tags of the legend ('~': { floor: 'water' }); either stands in for floorTex.\n\nA material is `{ color, pattern, ...the pattern's numbers, ramp, glow, over }`. Its five tones come from `E.tones(color)`\n(or its own `ramp` of five, dark to light); the light picks a band, the pattern moves it a step, so a material works on\nevery surface and in every palette and recolors with one hex. An unknown name warns with the list of names.\nOverlays, the last on top, each in its own color's tones: `over: [['moss', '#5f7a3a', { up: .6 }], ['cracks']]`; moss on\nwhat looks up, cracks (the material a step darker), dirt near the ground (h 6), rust; each takes amount and size.\n\n| Pattern | Numbers | What |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| none | | the light alone |\n| planks | bw 3, len 14, dir | boards with joints; staves on round parts; dir: 'v' turns them |\n| crate | frame 2, bw 3 | a framed, braced side; planks on its lid |\n| bricks | bw 6, bh 3, mortar | running bond |\n| stones | size 5 | irregular stones (Voronoi), dark joints, a lit rim |\n| tiles | size 4 | square tiles, grout |\n| speck, noise | amount .08; scale 4 | specks; soft patches |\n| foliage | size 3.5 | leaf clumps lit on top |\n| bark | | fissures; rings on a cut end |\n| metal | rivet | a shine where lit; rivets |\n| cloth | fold .9 | weave and folds |\n| glaze | | a glossy shine |\n| thatch, shingles | course; bw | straw courses; roof tiles |\n\nYour own pattern: `E.PATTERNS.waves = (s, m) => Math.sin(s.u / (m.size || 3)) > .8 ? 1 : 0` (s.u, s.v: world units\nacross and up the surface; s.lid, s.curved, s.lit, s.W, s.H; return a step, -1 to +2). A material may also paint one kind\nof surface its own way, per pixel: `face(wx, z, tones, type, cx, cy, fi, nh, h)` or `roof(wx, wy, tones, type)` returning\na color or null, `floor(x, y, tag, view)` returning [r, g, b].\n\n## Write one\nE.tex = {\n  /** stone flagstones with running-bond rows. pal: {stones:[hex..], mortar, hi, lo, speck} */\n  flagstone(x, y, pal, size = 16) {\n    const row = Math.floor(y / size), off = (row & 1) * size / 2, col = Math.floor((x + off) / size), lx = x + off - col * size, ly = y - row * size;\n    if (lx < 1 || ly < 1) return pal.mortar;\n    const h = hash2(col, row); let c = pal.stones[(h * pal.stones.length) | 0];\n    if (lx < 2 || ly < 2) c = pal.hi; else if (lx > size - 1.5 || ly > size - 1.5) c = pal.lo;\n    const n = hash2(Math.floor(x * 1.3), Math.floor(y * 1.3)); if (n < .05) c = pal.speck;\n    if (h > .93 && lx > 3 && lx < size - 3 && Math.abs(lx - ly * .7 - 3) < .6) c = pal.mortar;\n    return c;\n  },\n  /** grass with darker tufts and a few flowers. o: { base, dark, light, flower } hex colors */\n  grass(x, y, o = {}) {\n    // blotches of light and dark grass at two scales, short blade marks, rare flower clusters (no single-pixel static)\n    const n = noise2(x * .07, y * .07) * .65 + noise2(x * .23, y * .23) * .35, blade = noise2(x * .9, y * .35);\n    const fl = noise2(x * .12 + 40, y * .12 + 40), fh = hash2(Math.floor(x / 2), Math.floor(y / 2));\n    if (fl > .82 && fh > .8) return hex(fh > .93 ? (o.flower || '#f4e27a') : (o.flower2 || '#f2f2f6'));\n    if (n > .66 || (blade > .78 && n > .5)) return hex(o.dark || '#3e8a3a');\n    if (n < .34 || blade < .16) return hex(o.light || '#6cc25a');\n    return hex(o.base || '#55a94a');\n  },\n  /** dirt, sand or snow: base color with soft noise and specks. o: { base, dark, light } */\n  dirt(x, y, o = {}) {\n    // soft patches plus small pebbles (2-3 px clusters with a lit edge), no static\n    const n = noise2(x * .1, y * .1) * .7 + noise2(x * .3, y * .3) * .3, peb = noise2(x * .45 + 9, y * .45 + 3);\n    if (peb > .84) return hex(noise2(x * .45 + 9, (y - 1) * .45 + 3) > .84 ? (o.dark || '#6e4a2e') : (o.light || '#c9a276'));\n    return hex(n > .62 ? (o.light || '#b08a5e') : n < .3 ? (o.dark || '#7d5838') : (o.base || '#9a7048'));\n  },\n  /** water with static ripple lines (baked, so it does not move). o: { base, dark, light } */\n  water(x, y, o = {}) {\n    const w = Math.sin(x * .35 + Math.sin(y * .18) * 2.2 + y * .05);\n    if (w > .93 && ((Math.floor(x) + Math.floor(y)) & 1)) return hex(o.light || '#9fe3ff');\n    return hex(noise2(x * .05, y * .05) > .55 ? (o.base || '#2f7fd0') : (o.dark || '#2464b0'));\n  },\n  /** wooden floor boards running along x. o: { base, dark, line } */\n  planks(x, y, o = {}) {\n    const row = Math.floor(y / 6), ly = y - row * 6, len = 20 + Math.floor(hash2(row, 3) * 18), joint = (x + row * 13) % len;\n    if (ly < 1 || joint < 1) return hex(o.line || '#4a2e1c');\n    const g = hash2(Math.floor(x / 3), row); return hex(g > .7 ? (o.dark || '#8a5a34') : (o.base || '#9d6a3f'));\n  },\n  /** checkerboard tiles (castle floors, bonus rooms). o: { a, b, size } */\n  checker(x, y, o = {}) { const s = o.size || 16; return hex(((Math.floor(x / s) + Math.floor(y / s)) & 1) ? (o.a || '#d8d0e8') : (o.b || '#5a5270')); },\n  /** plain color with light noise, for roads, carpets and space floors. o: { base, amount } */\n  plain(x, y, o = {}) { const c = hex(o.base || '#4a4458'), k = 1 + (Math.round((noise2(x * .15, y * .15) - .5) * 4) / 4) * (o.amount === undefined ? .14 : o.amount); return c.map(v => v * k); }\n};\n\nbarrel crate chest table chair stool bench bed bookcase shelf pot jar sack cart well sign lamppost anvil fence pine tree bush grass rock crystal\nbrick stone rock plank timber plaster hedge speckle plain tiles slab leaves grass flagstone dirt water planks checker wood metal ground pipe block bonus oak walnut birch crate cobble marble granite sandstone slate iron steel gold copper bronze clay glazed porcelain linen burlap wool velvet leather bark needles shrub moss straw sand snow mud shingle bone ice crystal flame ruin rusted","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Y3CrCyNn8YYjUyjGVXPFNf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf9JbNcVG5Tf64V1a29t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3672,"cache_read_input_tokens":120194,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3672,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8704baa7-6f68-414d-afec-f55fd2d8121c","uuid":"66345f8a-ee7b-428e-8bab-eb757f2df944","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:41:22.863Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf9Jb2XpoK6XwQY3BVp5","thinking_duration_ms":822,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf9JbNcVG5Tf64V1a29t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the world: the town map, the Superlab, and set dressing, all built from code."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3672,"cache_read_input_tokens":120194,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3672,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8704baa7-6f68-414d-afec-f55fd2d8121c","uuid":"eacfeefe-72f0-4c15-8feb-f082a839c7cb","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:41:22.864Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf9Jb2XpoK6XwQY3BVp5"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf9JbNcVG5Tf64V1a29t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014tzCVeXJ4fH9Gpj5qbR3wT","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-183711__xb81546/work/Walter-Whitewash-BreakingBad-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261102-183711/src/10-world.js","content":"// WALTER WHITEWASH: the places. Two maps built from code: Albuquerky (the town, the desert, the car wash, the RV) and the\n// Superlab (the last room). Also the people's looks and every line anyone says. Pure data, plus builders that need the engine.\n(() => {\nconst WW = (globalThis.WW = globalThis.WW || {});\nconst W = {};\n\n// ---- the town -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 48 x 34 cells of 16 units. '.' sand, 'r' road, 'p' sidewalk, 'w' wet concrete (car wash), '#' rim rocks. Buildings are\n// wall types: 1 house, 2 school, 3 rim rock, 4 RV, 5 car wash, 6 supply store, 7 Los Polluelos, 8 fence\nW.COLS = 48; W.ROWS = 34;\nW.townRows = () => {\n  const g = Array.from({ length: W.ROWS }, () => Array(W.COLS).fill('.'));\n  const fill = (x0, y0, x1, y1, ch) => { for (let y = y0; y <= y1; y++) for (let x = x0; x <= x1; x++) g[y][x] = ch; };\n  const put = (x, y, ch) => { g[y][x] = ch; };\n  // roads and sidewalks\n  fill(1, 13, 46, 17, 'p'); fill(1, 14, 46, 16, 'r'); fill(21, 1, 25, 32, 'p'); fill(22, 1, 24, 32, 'r'); fill(21, 13, 25, 17, 'p'); fill(22, 13, 24, 17, 'r');\n  fill(1, 14, 46, 16, 'r');\n  // sidewalks in front of the buildings\n  fill(2, 10, 15, 10, 'p'); fill(28, 10, 36, 10, 'p'); fill(38, 10, 46, 10, 'p'); fill(28, 27, 38, 27, 'p');\n  // buildings\n  fill(2, 2, 15, 9, '2'); fill(28, 2, 36, 8, '1'); fill(37, 2, 46, 9, '7'); fill(28, 19, 38, 26, '6');\n  fill(40, 21, 46, 24, '4');\n  // car wash: three walls, open to the south, wet floor, a counter spot\n  fill(2, 19, 14, 27, 'w'); fill(2, 19, 14, 19, '5'); fill(2, 19, 2, 27, '5'); fill(14, 19, 14, 27, '5');\n  fill(5, 19, 6, 20, '5');\n  // two bays divided by short walls, cars sit between them\n  fill(7, 24, 7, 26, '5'); fill(10, 24, 10, 26, '5');\n  // the rim\n  for (let x = 0; x < W.COLS; x++) { put(x, 0, '#'); put(x, W.ROWS - 1, '#'); }\n  for (let y = 0; y < W.ROWS; y++) { put(0, y, '#'); put(W.COLS - 1, y, '#'); }\n  // gaps for the roads through the rim stay closed: it is a closed town (the demo's whole world)\n  // fences\n  for (let x = 17; x <= 19; x++) put(x, 22, '8');\n  for (let x = 40; x <= 44; x++) put(x, 28, '8');\n  // spawns and stations (each overwrites one cell: the cell keeps its floor)\n  const S = { '@': [32, 11], H: [32, 11], T: [9, 11], P: [42, 11], M: [33, 28], C: [43, 26], J: [41, 26], W: [8, 22], L: [43, 31], n: [19, 3], o: [45, 12], u: [12, 31],\n    D: [8, 28] };\n  for (const [ch, [x, y]] of Object.entries(S)) if (ch !== 'H') put(x, y, ch);\n  const X = [[5, 12], [17, 12], [27, 12], [20, 29], [36, 12], [44, 18], [6, 31], [30, 31], [18, 18], [26, 18]];\n  for (const [x, y] of X) put(x, y, 'x');\n  const E = [[30, 31], [44, 30], [36, 30], [12, 30], [5, 17], [18, 25], [34, 17], [45, 19], [27, 29]];\n  for (const [x, y] of E) put(x, y, 'e');\n  for (const [x, y] of [[22, 2], [22, 31], [2, 15]]) put(x, y, 'c');\n  return g.map(r => r.join(''));\n};\nW.townLegend = {\n  '.': { floor: 'sand' }, r: { floor: 'road' }, p: { floor: 'walk' }, w: { floor: 'wet' },\n  '#': 3, 1: 1, 2: 2, 4: 4, 5: 5, 6: 6, 7: 7, 8: 8,\n  '@': { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'hero' }, T: { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'teacher' }, P: { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'gus' }, M: { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'shop' },\n  C: { floor: 'sand', spawn: 'cook' }, J: { floor: 'sand', spawn: 'jimmy' }, W: { floor: 'wet', spawn: 'counter' }, L: { floor: 'sand', spawn: 'hatch' },\n  n: { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'drop-north' }, o: { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'drop-east' }, u: { floor: 'sand', spawn: 'drop-south' }, D: { floor: 'wet', spawn: 'sol' },\n  x: { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'customer' }, e: { floor: 'sand', spawn: 'thug' }, c: { floor: 'road', spawn: 'cop' }\n};\nW.townTypes = {\n  1: { h: 34, top: '#a86a4a', side: '#d9b48a', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles' },\n  2: { h: 38, top: '#8a5a4a', side: '#a2573d', face: 'brick', roof: 'slab' },\n  3: { h: 26, top: '#8a6a4a', side: '#a07a52', face: 'rock', roof: 'plain' },\n  4: { h: 28, top: '#e8ecee', side: '#d4dadc', face: 'plain', roof: 'plain', line: '#4a9aa8' },\n  5: { h: 26, top: '#5fa0c8', side: '#c8dce8', face: 'plaster', roof: 'plain' },\n  6: { h: 32, top: '#6a6a72', side: '#c4a45a', face: 'plank', roof: 'slab' },\n  7: { h: 36, top: '#b8362a', side: '#f0c030', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles' },\n  8: { h: 9, top: '#8a6a4a', side: '#7a5a3a', face: 'plank', roof: 'plain' }\n};\nW.townFloor = (x, y, tag) => {\n  const E = My3D2dge, n = E.noise2(x * .1, y * .1), n2 = E.noise2(x * .33 + 7, y * .33 + 3);\n  if (tag === 'road') {\n    const c = 36 + Math.round(n * 12) + (n2 > .78 ? 8 : 0), line = Math.abs(y % 16 - 8) < .8 && Math.floor(x / 6) % 2 === 0 && y > 224 && y < 270;\n    const vline = Math.abs(x % 16 - 8) < .8 && Math.floor(y / 6) % 2 === 0 && x > 352 && x < 400;\n    return line || vline ? [226, 190, 60] : [c, c + 2, c + 8];\n  }\n  if (tag === 'walk') { const t = (Math.floor(x / 8) + Math.floor(y / 8)) & 1, e = x % 8 < 1 || y % 8 < 1; return e ? [118, 112, 104] : t ? [168, 160, 148] : [160, 152, 140]; }\n  if (tag === 'wet') { const e = x % 16 < 1 || y % 16 < 1; const s = n2 > .8 ? 26 : 0; return e ? [70, 96, 110] : [92 + s, 138 + s, 158 + s]; }\n  if (tag === 'lab') { const e = x % 16 < 1 || y % 16 < 1; return e ? [32, 38, 44] : ((Math.floor(x / 16) + Math.floor(y / 16)) & 1) ? [72, 84, 92] : [64, 76, 84]; }\n  // sand\n  const E2 = E.tex.dirt(x, y, { base: '#c79a5e', dark: '#b3874f', light: '#d8b074' });\n  return E2;\n};\n\n// dressing: [shape, x, y, options]. Solid ones block the way. Rocks and cactus are scenery in the desert.\nW.townDress = () => {\n  const out = [];\n  const s = (id, cx, cy, o = {}) => out.push([id, cx * 16 + 8, cy * 16 + 8, o]);\n  [[30, 29], [40, 30], [8, 31], [15, 29], [34, 31], [46, 28], [3, 30], [27, 25], [39, 18], [10, 17], [4, 17]].forEach(([x, y], i) => s('rock', x, y, { params: { r: 6 + (i % 3) * 2, seed: i + 1 } }));\n  [[17, 30], [41, 29], [2, 24], [18, 19], [26, 31], [45, 28]].forEach(([x, y], i) => s('bush', x, y, { params: { r: 6 + (i % 2) * 2 } }));\n  s('barrel', 30, 27, { solid: true }); s('barrel', 31, 27, { solid: true, facing: .6 }); s('crate', 37, 27, { solid: true }); s('crate', 36, 27, { solid: true, facing: .4 });\n  s('barrel', 17, 11); s('sign', 20, 12, { solid: false }); s('sack', 47 - 3, 11);\n  s('crate', 40, 20, { solid: true }); s('barrel', 41, 27, { solid: true });\n  s('cart', 5, 25, { solid: true, facing: 0 }); s('cart', 12, 25, { solid: true, facing: Math.PI }); s('barrel', 4, 21, { solid: true });\n  return out;\n};\n\n// ---- the Superlab ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nW.labRows = () => [\n  '########################',\n  '#......................#',\n  '#..#..................#.#',\n  '#..#....G.............#.#',\n  '#......................#.#',\n  '#....#..........#......#',\n  '#...............#......#',\n  '#.......tt.............#',\n  '#.......tt.............#',\n  '#....#..........#......#',\n  '#......................#',\n  '#..#..................#.#',\n  '#..#......@...........#.#',\n  '#......................#',\n  '########################'];\nW.labLegend = { '.': { floor: 'lab' }, '#': 1, t: { floor: 'lab', tile: 2 }, G: { floor: 'lab', spawn: 'boss' }, '@': { floor: 'lab', spawn: 'hero' } };\nW.labTypes = {\n  1: { h: 40, top: '#4a5560', side: '#6a7884', face: 'plain', roof: 'plain', line: '#2a3238' },\n  2: { h: 20, top: '#8ab8d8', side: '#5a8aa8', face: 'plain', roof: 'plain' }\n};\n\n// ---- people --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// each is a Humanoid spec. Walt wears the green shirt and the khaki; in the cook he is in the yellow suit.\nW.looks = {\n  walt:   { size: 1.2, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'bald', hat: { style: 'cap', color: '#2a2a2a' }, colors: { skin: '#e8c8b0', cloth: '#8a9a5a', pants: '#b8a070', boot: '#4a3a2a', hair: '#3a2a20' } },\n  waltgun:{ size: 1.2, build: 'chibi', weapon: 'gun', outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'bald', hat: { style: 'cap', color: '#2a2a2a' }, colors: { skin: '#e8c8b0', cloth: '#8a9a5a', pants: '#b8a070', boot: '#4a3a2a', metal: '#3a3a42' } },\n  hazmat: { size: 1.2, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'bald', hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#d8c020' }, colors: { skin: '#e8c8b0', cloth: '#e0c828', coat: '#e0c828', pants: '#d8c020', boot: '#2a2a2a', glove: '#2a2a2a' } },\n  jimmy:  { size: 1.15, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'short', hair: 'short', hat: { style: 'cap', color: '#d8d8d8' }, colors: { skin: '#e0b898', cloth: '#6a6ae0', pants: '#3a4a6a', hair: '#8a6a3a', boot: '#d8d8d8' } },\n  gus:    { size: 1.35, build: 'heroic', weapon: 'gun', outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'short', colors: { skin: '#d8b090', cloth: '#d8c8a8', coat: '#a8b4b8', pants: '#5a5a62', hair: '#6a5a4a', boot: '#2a2a2a', metal: '#2a2a32' } },\n  cop:    { size: 1.2, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'short', hair: 'short', hat: { style: 'cap', color: '#1a2a5a' }, colors: { skin: '#e0b898', cloth: '#3a5a98', pants: '#1a2a4a', boot: '#1a1a1a', hair: '#2a2a2a' } },\n  hank:   { size: 1.3, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'short', hair: 'short', colors: { skin: '#d8b090', cloth: '#d8d4c8', pants: '#3a3a3a', boot: '#1a1a1a', hair: '#2a2018' } },\n  thug:   { size: 1.2, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'none', hair: 'spiky', colors: { skin: '#b88a68', cloth: '#a8281c', pants: '#2a2a3a', boot: '#1a1a1a', hair: '#1a1a1a' } },\n  shooter:{ size: 1.2, build: 'chibi', weapon: 'gun', outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'ponytail', hat: { style: 'band', color: '#d8d8d8' }, colors: { skin: '#a87a58', cloth: '#6a1a8a', pants: '#2a2a3a', boot: '#1a1a1a', hair: '#1a1a1a' } },\n  enforcer:{ size: 1.45, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'bald', colors: { skin: '#a87a58', cloth: '#d8b020', coat: '#2a2a32', pants: '#1a1a1a', boot: '#0a0a0a' } },\n  teacher:{ size: 1.15, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'robe', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'long', colors: { skin: '#d8a888', cloth: '#9a4a7a', hair: '#4a2a2a' } },\n  sol:    { size: 1.15, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'short', colors: { skin: '#d8b090', cloth: '#d86a98', coat: '#e8e0c8', pants: '#3a2a4a', hair: '#3a2a20' } }\n};\nW.customerLook = i => {\n  const hairs = ['short', 'long', 'spiky', 'ponytail', 'bald'], cl = ['#c85a5a', '#5a8ac8', '#7ab85a', '#c8a85a', '#8a5ac8', '#5ac8b8', '#a0a0a8'], sk = ['#f0d0b8', '#d8a888', '#a87a58', '#7a5238', '#e8c8a8'];\n  return { size: 1.1, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: i % 3 === 0 ? 'robe' : 'shirt', sleeves: i % 2 ? 'long' : 'short', hair: hairs[i % hairs.length],\n    colors: { skin: sk[i % sk.length], cloth: cl[(i * 3) % cl.length], pants: '#4a4a5a', boot: '#2a2a2a', hair: ['#2a1a10', '#6a4a20', '#1a1a1a', '#a08a50'][i % 4] } };\n};\n\n// ---- the words ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Voices are gibberish (the game babbles each speaker at their own pitch), so the text carries it: dry, short, mean to itself.\nW.pitch = { walt: 150, jimmy: 260, gus: 120, cop: 200, hank: 135, thug: 170, teacher: 300, sol: 230, customer: 240, narrator: 190, enforcer: 95 };\nW.names = { walt: 'WALT', jimmy: 'JIMMY', gus: 'GUS FRYING', cop: 'OFFICER', hank: 'HANK SCHRODINGER', thug: 'THUG', teacher: 'MS. CHALKWELL', sol: 'SOL GOODGIRL', customer: 'CUSTOMER', narrator: '', enforcer: 'ENFORCER' };\n\nW.script = {\n  intro: [\n    ['narrator', 'Albuquerky, New Mexico. A Tuesday that looked like all the others.'],\n    ['walt', 'Fifty-two years old. Sixteen years teaching chemistry to kids who would rather be asleep. A second job at a car wash, wiping down other people\\'s Hondas.'],\n    ['walt', 'And now the doctor says I have a cough that is not a cough. The bills are $600 a day, and they do not care that I am a nice man.'],\n    ['walt', 'I know chemistry. Better than anyone in this state. It is time to put it to work.'],\n    ['walt', 'Eighteen thousand dollars, clean, in five days. That is the number. Cook, sell, launder. And be home for dinner.']\n  ],\n  teacher: [\n    ['teacher', 'Walter! You are in early. The students will be so excited to see you. Okay, no, that was a lie. But I am glad you are here.'],\n    ['walt', 'I am only passing by, Ms. Chalkwell. I forgot my pens.'],\n    ['teacher', 'You look tired. Have you been to see anyone?'],\n    ['walt', 'I have been to see everyone.']\n  ],\n  jimmyFirst: [\n    ['jimmy', 'Yo, Mr. White-wash! You came! I knew it, I told everyone, I said Mr. Whitewash is gonna cook. Bro, this RV is so sick.'],\n    ['walt', 'Jimmy. Never say my name out loud. And it is not \"sick.\" It is a mobile laboratory with a leak in the roof.'],\n    ['jimmy', 'Okay, okay. So, you buy the stuff at the supply store, bring it here, and we cook. I handle the, uh, vibes.'],\n    ['walt', 'You handle the vibes. Fine. Measure, heat, filter. We do this the right way, or we do not do this.']\n  ],\n  jimmyNoStuff: [\n    ['jimmy', 'Yo. Uh. We need ingredients first. Supply store, down the road. Eight hundred a batch. Bring it and I will be here, being supportive.']\n  ],\n  jimmyTips: [\n    [['jimmy', 'Sell it to the corner guys. Anybody with a dollar sign over their head. Do not do it in front of a cop. Pretty sure that is in the rules.']],\n    [['jimmy', 'The car wash takes a quarter. A quarter! Sol says it is a \"very reasonable laundering coefficient.\" Whatever that means.']],\n    [['jimmy', 'Better purity, better price. Ninety-nine percent is blue. Blue is, like, a brand. You are a brand, Mr. White-wash.']],\n    [['jimmy', 'Rivals hang out in the desert. If they come at you, hit them with your wrench. Or the pistol. I would pick the pistol.']]\n  ],\n  solFirst: [\n    ['sol', 'Walter Whitewash! The man, the myth, the cough. Sol Goodgirl, attorney at car wash. Do you have a minute? Or, more importantly, do you have a minimum?'],\n    ['walt', 'I have a lot of money that is not exactly mine, and a need for it to become mine.'],\n    ['sol', 'Beautiful. Hand it to me in the bay, I will say it was a very busy week for hot wax. I keep a quarter. The government keeps the rest of its questions.'],\n    ['sol', 'Two grand a day through the front bays. We add bays, we add grand. It is a growth industry.']\n  ],\n  solWelcome: [['sol', 'Welcome back to the Whitewash Auto Spa. Where everything comes out clean. Everything.']],\n  gus: [\n    [['gus', 'Mr. Whitewash. Sit. Eat. The chicken is excellent. Everything I do is excellent.'],\n     ['gus', 'I have heard of your product. They say it is blue. I do not believe it. Prove it. Three bricks at seventy percent, by the east gate.'],\n     ['walt', 'And if I do?'], ['gus', 'Then we will talk about what it is you want. Everyone wants something.']],\n    [['gus', 'Mr. Whitewash. Good. You are punctual. I respect that.'],\n     ['gus', 'My organization has a problem. A rival crew from the desert is cutting into my corners. They are loud. I do not like loud.'],\n     ['walt', 'And you want me to handle it?'], ['gus', 'I want you to cook. The crew will handle itself, in time.']],\n    [['gus', 'You have a visitor. A DEA agent named Schrodinger has been parked outside the restaurant. He is on the phone with his wife. It is... touching.'],\n     ['walt', 'Hank is my brother-in-law.'], ['gus', 'Then be careful at the dinner table. His coffee is better than his instincts.']],\n    [['gus', 'Four days. You have the numbers, I have mine. Between us we could own this city.'],\n     ['walt', 'I am not interested in owning a city. I am interested in paying for a hospital.'], ['gus', 'Of course. That is what everyone says. Then the money starts to taste good.']],\n    [['gus', 'It is the last day. I think you know what comes next. I have a laboratory under the desert. A hundred and fifty thousand dollars a day. It is yours, if you come to work for me.'],\n     ['walt', 'And if I say no?'], ['gus', 'You will not say no. Come down. See it.']]\n  ],\n  gusReturn: [['gus', 'I am a patient man. But even I have a calendar.'], ['gus', 'Bring me the product, Mr. Whitewash. Not excuses.']],\n  gusPaid: [['gus', 'Impeccable. As promised. The rest is in the envelope. Please, take some chicken.']],\n  gusNoStuff: [['gus', 'You do not have what I asked for. We will not discuss anything else.']],\n  hank: [['hank', 'Walter! Hey! Haha. You look like a guy who has not slept. Are you okay? Skyler says you have been cooking late. At the car wash? Seriously?'],\n         ['walt', 'I have a lot on my plate, Hank.'], ['hank', 'We should have the boys over. Barbecue. I will bring the Schrader. I mean the, uh, Schrodinger. Still working on the name.']],\n  hatch: [['gus', '(Through the intercom) Come down, Mr. Whitewash. The door is open.'], ['walt', 'This is it. Down the ladder, into the hole in the ground.']],\n  hatchShut: [['walt', 'The hatch is welded shut. Whatever is down there, I am not ready for it. Not yet. Not until the money is in the bank, or the calendar runs out.']],\n  bossIntro: [\n    ['gus', 'You cook very well, Mr. Whitewash. But this is a business. And a business does not tolerate a man who thinks he is the owner.'],\n    ['walt', 'I am not the owner. I am the one who knocks.'],\n    ['gus', 'Then knock.']],\n  bossHalf: [['gus', 'You are making this unnecessarily untidy.'], ['walt', 'Say my name.']],\n  bossDown: [['gus', 'Do you know what it costs, to be a man like me?'], ['walt', 'I am not in danger, Gus. I am the danger.']],\n  endWin: [\n    ['narrator', 'The Superlab went quiet. Somewhere above, in the desert, a rattlesnake crossed the road and nobody stopped to watch.'],\n    ['walt', 'I did it. I did all of it. And I did it for the family.'],\n    ['narrator', 'That is what he told himself.']],\n  endLate: [['narrator', 'Day Five ended. The clock ran out before the Superlab did. Albuquerky does not wait for a cough.']],\n  bust: [['cop', 'Sir, step away from the RV. We have received a number of calls about a smell.'], ['walt', 'It is a chemistry experiment.'], ['cop', 'That is what they all say.']],\n  customerBuy: [['customer', 'Yo. You the guy? The blue guy? I heard about you. I need one.']],\n  customerNo: [['customer', 'You got nothin\\'? Come on, man. Do not waste my time.']],\n  customerHappy: [['customer', 'Oh man. Oh MAN. That is beautiful.']],\n  noMoney: [['walt', 'I cannot afford that.']],\n  needBricks: [['walt', 'I have nothing to sell. The bricks are the product. The product is the bricks.']],\n  noIngredients: [['walt', 'No ingredients. I need a batch from the supply store before Jimmy and I can cook.']],\n  tooLate: [['walt', 'It is too dark to cook. Even I need sleep. Home. Bed.']],\n  tutorial: [\n    ['Move', 'Left stick or WASD. Walk to the glowing markers. Press the interact button on any marker to use it.'],\n    ['The loop', 'Buy ingredients at the supply store, cook at the RV, sell to the corner customers, launder at the car wash.'],\n    ['Heat', 'Cops notice you when the heat is high or you do anything loud. Break their line of sight to cool off.'],\n    ['Fight', 'Square / J / click hits. Hold aim and shoot with the pistol. Triangle / Q switches weapon.']\n  ]\n};\n\n// the day summary and the one-liners at day's end\nW.dayLines = ['A day like any other, which is the problem.', 'The numbers are moving. So is the cough.', 'Everybody has a limit. Yours has not arrived yet.', 'Four days in. You do not recognise the man in the mirror.', 'Tomorrow is the last day.'];\n\nWW.world = W;\nif (typeof module !== 'undefined') module.exports = W;\n})();\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3672,"cache_read_input_tokens":120194,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3672,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8704baa7-6f68-414d-afec-f55fd2d8121c","uuid":"029e8606-310f-40d8-b934-1fb9bfb7a04c","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:42:29.625Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf9Jb2XpoK6XwQY3BVp5","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014tzCVeXJ4fH9Gpj5qbR3wT":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-183711__xb81546/work/Walter-Whitewash-BreakingBad-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261102-183711/src/10-world.js","content":"// WALTER WHITEWASH: the places. Two maps built from code: Albuquerky (the town, the desert, the car wash, the RV) and the\n// Superlab (the last room). Also the people's looks and every line anyone says. Pure data, plus builders that need the engine.\n(() => {\nconst WW = (globalThis.WW = globalThis.WW || {});\nconst W = {};\n\n// ---- the town -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 48 x 34 cells of 16 units. '.' sand, 'r' road, 'p' sidewalk, 'w' wet concrete (car wash), '#' rim rocks. Buildings are\n// wall types: 1 house, 2 school, 3 rim rock, 4 RV, 5 car wash, 6 supply store, 7 Los Polluelos, 8 fence\nW.COLS = 48; W.ROWS = 34;\nW.townRows = () => {\n  const g = Array.from({ length: W.ROWS }, () => Array(W.COLS).fill('.'));\n  const fill = (x0, y0, x1, y1, ch) => { for (let y = y0; y <= y1; y++) for (let x = x0; x <= x1; x++) g[y][x] = ch; };\n  const put = (x, y, ch) => { g[y][x] = ch; };\n  // roads and sidewalks\n  fill(1, 13, 46, 17, 'p'); fill(1, 14, 46, 16, 'r'); fill(21, 1, 25, 32, 'p'); fill(22, 1, 24, 32, 'r'); fill(21, 13, 25, 17, 'p'); fill(22, 13, 24, 17, 'r');\n  fill(1, 14, 46, 16, 'r');\n  // sidewalks in front of the buildings\n  fill(2, 10, 15, 10, 'p'); fill(28, 10, 36, 10, 'p'); fill(38, 10, 46, 10, 'p'); fill(28, 27, 38, 27, 'p');\n  // buildings\n  fill(2, 2, 15, 9, '2'); fill(28, 2, 36, 8, '1'); fill(37, 2, 46, 9, '7'); fill(28, 19, 38, 26, '6');\n  fill(40, 21, 46, 24, '4');\n  // car wash: three walls, open to the south, wet floor, a counter spot\n  fill(2, 19, 14, 27, 'w'); fill(2, 19, 14, 19, '5'); fill(2, 19, 2, 27, '5'); fill(14, 19, 14, 27, '5');\n  fill(5, 19, 6, 20, '5');\n  // two bays divided by short walls, cars sit between them\n  fill(7, 24, 7, 26, '5'); fill(10, 24, 10, 26, '5');\n  // the rim\n  for (let x = 0; x < W.COLS; x++) { put(x, 0, '#'); put(x, W.ROWS - 1, '#'); }\n  for (let y = 0; y < W.ROWS; y++) { put(0, y, '#'); put(W.COLS - 1, y, '#'); }\n  // gaps for the roads through the rim stay closed: it is a closed town (the demo's whole world)\n  // fences\n  for (let x = 17; x <= 19; x++) put(x, 22, '8');\n  for (let x = 40; x <= 44; x++) put(x, 28, '8');\n  // spawns and stations (each overwrites one cell: the cell keeps its floor)\n  const S = { '@': [32, 11], H: [32, 11], T: [9, 11], P: [42, 11], M: [33, 28], C: [43, 26], J: [41, 26], W: [8, 22], L: [43, 31], n: [19, 3], o: [45, 12], u: [12, 31],\n    D: [8, 28] };\n  for (const [ch, [x, y]] of Object.entries(S)) if (ch !== 'H') put(x, y, ch);\n  const X = [[5, 12], [17, 12], [27, 12], [20, 29], [36, 12], [44, 18], [6, 31], [30, 31], [18, 18], [26, 18]];\n  for (const [x, y] of X) put(x, y, 'x');\n  const E = [[30, 31], [44, 30], [36, 30], [12, 30], [5, 17], [18, 25], [34, 17], [45, 19], [27, 29]];\n  for (const [x, y] of E) put(x, y, 'e');\n  for (const [x, y] of [[22, 2], [22, 31], [2, 15]]) put(x, y, 'c');\n  return g.map(r => r.join(''));\n};\nW.townLegend = {\n  '.': { floor: 'sand' }, r: { floor: 'road' }, p: { floor: 'walk' }, w: { floor: 'wet' },\n  '#': 3, 1: 1, 2: 2, 4: 4, 5: 5, 6: 6, 7: 7, 8: 8,\n  '@': { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'hero' }, T: { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'teacher' }, P: { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'gus' }, M: { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'shop' },\n  C: { floor: 'sand', spawn: 'cook' }, J: { floor: 'sand', spawn: 'jimmy' }, W: { floor: 'wet', spawn: 'counter' }, L: { floor: 'sand', spawn: 'hatch' },\n  n: { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'drop-north' }, o: { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'drop-east' }, u: { floor: 'sand', spawn: 'drop-south' }, D: { floor: 'wet', spawn: 'sol' },\n  x: { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'customer' }, e: { floor: 'sand', spawn: 'thug' }, c: { floor: 'road', spawn: 'cop' }\n};\nW.townTypes = {\n  1: { h: 34, top: '#a86a4a', side: '#d9b48a', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles' },\n  2: { h: 38, top: '#8a5a4a', side: '#a2573d', face: 'brick', roof: 'slab' },\n  3: { h: 26, top: '#8a6a4a', side: '#a07a52', face: 'rock', roof: 'plain' },\n  4: { h: 28, top: '#e8ecee', side: '#d4dadc', face: 'plain', roof: 'plain', line: '#4a9aa8' },\n  5: { h: 26, top: '#5fa0c8', side: '#c8dce8', face: 'plaster', roof: 'plain' },\n  6: { h: 32, top: '#6a6a72', side: '#c4a45a', face: 'plank', roof: 'slab' },\n  7: { h: 36, top: '#b8362a', side: '#f0c030', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles' },\n  8: { h: 9, top: '#8a6a4a', side: '#7a5a3a', face: 'plank', roof: 'plain' }\n};\nW.townFloor = (x, y, tag) => {\n  const E = My3D2dge, n = E.noise2(x * .1, y * .1), n2 = E.noise2(x * .33 + 7, y * .33 + 3);\n  if (tag === 'road') {\n    const c = 36 + Math.round(n * 12) + (n2 > .78 ? 8 : 0), line = Math.abs(y % 16 - 8) < .8 && Math.floor(x / 6) % 2 === 0 && y > 224 && y < 270;\n    const vline = Math.abs(x % 16 - 8) < .8 && Math.floor(y / 6) % 2 === 0 && x > 352 && x < 400;\n    return line || vline ? [226, 190, 60] : [c, c + 2, c + 8];\n  }\n  if (tag === 'walk') { const t = (Math.floor(x / 8) + Math.floor(y / 8)) & 1, e = x % 8 < 1 || y % 8 < 1; return e ? [118, 112, 104] : t ? [168, 160, 148] : [160, 152, 140]; }\n  if (tag === 'wet') { const e = x % 16 < 1 || y % 16 < 1; const s = n2 > .8 ? 26 : 0; return e ? [70, 96, 110] : [92 + s, 138 + s, 158 + s]; }\n  if (tag === 'lab') { const e = x % 16 < 1 || y % 16 < 1; return e ? [32, 38, 44] : ((Math.floor(x / 16) + Math.floor(y / 16)) & 1) ? [72, 84, 92] : [64, 76, 84]; }\n  // sand\n  const E2 = E.tex.dirt(x, y, { base: '#c79a5e', dark: '#b3874f', light: '#d8b074' });\n  return E2;\n};\n\n// dressing: [shape, x, y, options]. Solid ones block the way. Rocks and cactus are scenery in the desert.\nW.townDress = () => {\n  const out = [];\n  const s = (id, cx, cy, o = {}) => out.push([id, cx * 16 + 8, cy * 16 + 8, o]);\n  [[30, 29], [40, 30], [8, 31], [15, 29], [34, 31], [46, 28], [3, 30], [27, 25], [39, 18], [10, 17], [4, 17]].forEach(([x, y], i) => s('rock', x, y, { params: { r: 6 + (i % 3) * 2, seed: i + 1 } }));\n  [[17, 30], [41, 29], [2, 24], [18, 19], [26, 31], [45, 28]].forEach(([x, y], i) => s('bush', x, y, { params: { r: 6 + (i % 2) * 2 } }));\n  s('barrel', 30, 27, { solid: true }); s('barrel', 31, 27, { solid: true, facing: .6 }); s('crate', 37, 27, { solid: true }); s('crate', 36, 27, { solid: true, facing: .4 });\n  s('barrel', 17, 11); s('sign', 20, 12, { solid: false }); s('sack', 47 - 3, 11);\n  s('crate', 40, 20, { solid: true }); s('barrel', 41, 27, { solid: true });\n  s('cart', 5, 25, { solid: true, facing: 0 }); s('cart', 12, 25, { solid: true, facing: Math.PI }); s('barrel', 4, 21, { solid: true });\n  return out;\n};\n\n// ---- the Superlab ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nW.labRows = () => [\n  '########################',\n  '#......................#',\n  '#..#..................#.#',\n  '#..#....G.............#.#',\n  '#......................#.#',\n  '#....#..........#......#',\n  '#...............#......#',\n  '#.......tt.............#',\n  '#.......tt.............#',\n  '#....#..........#......#',\n  '#......................#',\n  '#..#..................#.#',\n  '#..#......@...........#.#',\n  '#......................#',\n  '########################'];\nW.labLegend = { '.': { floor: 'lab' }, '#': 1, t: { floor: 'lab', tile: 2 }, G: { floor: 'lab', spawn: 'boss' }, '@': { floor: 'lab', spawn: 'hero' } };\nW.labTypes = {\n  1: { h: 40, top: '#4a5560', side: '#6a7884', face: 'plain', roof: 'plain', line: '#2a3238' },\n  2: { h: 20, top: '#8ab8d8', side: '#5a8aa8', face: 'plain', roof: 'plain' }\n};\n\n// ---- people --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// each is a Humanoid spec. Walt wears the green shirt and the khaki; in the cook he is in the yellow suit.\nW.looks = {\n  walt:   { size: 1.2, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'bald', hat: { style: 'cap', color: '#2a2a2a' }, colors: { skin: '#e8c8b0', cloth: '#8a9a5a', pants: '#b8a070', boot: '#4a3a2a', hair: '#3a2a20' } },\n  waltgun:{ size: 1.2, build: 'chibi', weapon: 'gun', outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'bald', hat: { style: 'cap', color: '#2a2a2a' }, colors: { skin: '#e8c8b0', cloth: '#8a9a5a', pants: '#b8a070', boot: '#4a3a2a', metal: '#3a3a42' } },\n  hazmat: { size: 1.2, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'bald', hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#d8c020' }, colors: { skin: '#e8c8b0', cloth: '#e0c828', coat: '#e0c828', pants: '#d8c020', boot: '#2a2a2a', glove: '#2a2a2a' } },\n  jimmy:  { size: 1.15, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'short', hair: 'short', hat: { style: 'cap', color: '#d8d8d8' }, colors: { skin: '#e0b898', cloth: '#6a6ae0', pants: '#3a4a6a', hair: '#8a6a3a', boot: '#d8d8d8' } },\n  gus:    { size: 1.35, build: 'heroic', weapon: 'gun', outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'short', colors: { skin: '#d8b090', cloth: '#d8c8a8', coat: '#a8b4b8', pants: '#5a5a62', hair: '#6a5a4a', boot: '#2a2a2a', metal: '#2a2a32' } },\n  cop:    { size: 1.2, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'short', hair: 'short', hat: { style: 'cap', color: '#1a2a5a' }, colors: { skin: '#e0b898', cloth: '#3a5a98', pants: '#1a2a4a', boot: '#1a1a1a', hair: '#2a2a2a' } },\n  hank:   { size: 1.3, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'short', hair: 'short', colors: { skin: '#d8b090', cloth: '#d8d4c8', pants: '#3a3a3a', boot: '#1a1a1a', hair: '#2a2018' } },\n  thug:   { size: 1.2, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'none', hair: 'spiky', colors: { skin: '#b88a68', cloth: '#a8281c', pants: '#2a2a3a', boot: '#1a1a1a', hair: '#1a1a1a' } },\n  shooter:{ size: 1.2, build: 'chibi', weapon: 'gun', outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'ponytail', hat: { style: 'band', color: '#d8d8d8' }, colors: { skin: '#a87a58', cloth: '#6a1a8a', pants: '#2a2a3a', boot: '#1a1a1a', hair: '#1a1a1a' } },\n  enforcer:{ size: 1.45, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'bald', colors: { skin: '#a87a58', cloth: '#d8b020', coat: '#2a2a32', pants: '#1a1a1a', boot: '#0a0a0a' } },\n  teacher:{ size: 1.15, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'robe', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'long', colors: { skin: '#d8a888', cloth: '#9a4a7a', hair: '#4a2a2a' } },\n  sol:    { size: 1.15, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'short', colors: { skin: '#d8b090', cloth: '#d86a98', coat: '#e8e0c8', pants: '#3a2a4a', hair: '#3a2a20' } }\n};\nW.customerLook = i => {\n  const hairs = ['short', 'long', 'spiky', 'ponytail', 'bald'], cl = ['#c85a5a', '#5a8ac8', '#7ab85a', '#c8a85a', '#8a5ac8', '#5ac8b8', '#a0a0a8'], sk = ['#f0d0b8', '#d8a888', '#a87a58', '#7a5238', '#e8c8a8'];\n  return { size: 1.1, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: i % 3 === 0 ? 'robe' : 'shirt', sleeves: i % 2 ? 'long' : 'short', hair: hairs[i % hairs.length],\n    colors: { skin: sk[i % sk.length], cloth: cl[(i * 3) % cl.length], pants: '#4a4a5a', boot: '#2a2a2a', hair: ['#2a1a10', '#6a4a20', '#1a1a1a', '#a08a50'][i % 4] } };\n};\n\n// ---- the words ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Voices are gibberish (the game babbles each speaker at their own pitch), so the text carries it: dry, short, mean to itself.\nW.pitch = { walt: 150, jimmy: 260, gus: 120, cop: 200, hank: 135, thug: 170, teacher: 300, sol: 230, customer: 240, narrator: 190, enforcer: 95 };\nW.names = { walt: 'WALT', jimmy: 'JIMMY', gus: 'GUS FRYING', cop: 'OFFICER', hank: 'HANK SCHRODINGER', thug: 'THUG', teacher: 'MS. CHALKWELL', sol: 'SOL GOODGIRL', customer: 'CUSTOMER', narrator: '', enforcer: 'ENFORCER' };\n\nW.script = {\n  intro: [\n    ['narrator', 'Albuquerky, New Mexico. A Tuesday that looked like all the others.'],\n    ['walt', 'Fifty-two years old. Sixteen years teaching chemistry to kids who would rather be asleep. A second job at a car wash, wiping down other people\\'s Hondas.'],\n    ['walt', 'And now the doctor says I have a cough that is not a cough. The bills are $600 a day, and they do not care that I am a nice man.'],\n    ['walt', 'I know chemistry. Better than anyone in this state. It is time to put it to work.'],\n    ['walt', 'Eighteen thousand dollars, clean, in five days. That is the number. Cook, sell, launder. And be home for dinner.']\n  ],\n  teacher: [\n    ['teacher', 'Walter! You are in early. The students will be so excited to see you. Okay, no, that was a lie. But I am glad you are here.'],\n    ['walt', 'I am only passing by, Ms. Chalkwell. I forgot my pens.'],\n    ['teacher', 'You look tired. Have you been to see anyone?'],\n    ['walt', 'I have been to see everyone.']\n  ],\n  jimmyFirst: [\n    ['jimmy', 'Yo, Mr. White-wash! You came! I knew it, I told everyone, I said Mr. Whitewash is gonna cook. Bro, this RV is so sick.'],\n    ['walt', 'Jimmy. Never say my name out loud. And it is not \"sick.\" It is a mobile laboratory with a leak in the roof.'],\n    ['jimmy', 'Okay, okay. So, you buy the stuff at the supply store, bring it here, and we cook. I handle the, uh, vibes.'],\n    ['walt', 'You handle the vibes. Fine. Measure, heat, filter. We do this the right way, or we do not do this.']\n  ],\n  jimmyNoStuff: [\n    ['jimmy', 'Yo. Uh. We need ingredients first. Supply store, down the road. Eight hundred a batch. Bring it and I will be here, being supportive.']\n  ],\n  jimmyTips: [\n    [['jimmy', 'Sell it to the corner guys. Anybody with a dollar sign over their head. Do not do it in front of a cop. Pretty sure that is in the rules.']],\n    [['jimmy', 'The car wash takes a quarter. A quarter! Sol says it is a \"very reasonable laundering coefficient.\" Whatever that means.']],\n    [['jimmy', 'Better purity, better price. Ninety-nine percent is blue. Blue is, like, a brand. You are a brand, Mr. White-wash.']],\n    [['jimmy', 'Rivals hang out in the desert. If they come at you, hit them with your wrench. Or the pistol. I would pick the pistol.']]\n  ],\n  solFirst: [\n    ['sol', 'Walter Whitewash! The man, the myth, the cough. Sol Goodgirl, attorney at car wash. Do you have a minute? Or, more importantly, do you have a minimum?'],\n    ['walt', 'I have a lot of money that is not exactly mine, and a need for it to become mine.'],\n    ['sol', 'Beautiful. Hand it to me in the bay, I will say it was a very busy week for hot wax. I keep a quarter. The government keeps the rest of its questions.'],\n    ['sol', 'Two grand a day through the front bays. We add bays, we add grand. It is a growth industry.']\n  ],\n  solWelcome: [['sol', 'Welcome back to the Whitewash Auto Spa. Where everything comes out clean. Everything.']],\n  gus: [\n    [['gus', 'Mr. Whitewash. Sit. Eat. The chicken is excellent. Everything I do is excellent.'],\n     ['gus', 'I have heard of your product. They say it is blue. I do not believe it. Prove it. Three bricks at seventy percent, by the east gate.'],\n     ['walt', 'And if I do?'], ['gus', 'Then we will talk about what it is you want. Everyone wants something.']],\n    [['gus', 'Mr. Whitewash. Good. You are punctual. I respect that.'],\n     ['gus', 'My organization has a problem. A rival crew from the desert is cutting into my corners. They are loud. I do not like loud.'],\n     ['walt', 'And you want me to handle it?'], ['gus', 'I want you to cook. The crew will handle itself, in time.']],\n    [['gus', 'You have a visitor. A DEA agent named Schrodinger has been parked outside the restaurant. He is on the phone with his wife. It is... touching.'],\n     ['walt', 'Hank is my brother-in-law.'], ['gus', 'Then be careful at the dinner table. His coffee is better than his instincts.']],\n    [['gus', 'Four days. You have the numbers, I have mine. Between us we could own this city.'],\n     ['walt', 'I am not interested in owning a city. I am interested in paying for a hospital.'], ['gus', 'Of course. That is what everyone says. Then the money starts to taste good.']],\n    [['gus', 'It is the last day. I think you know what comes next. I have a laboratory under the desert. A hundred and fifty thousand dollars a day. It is yours, if you come to work for me.'],\n     ['walt', 'And if I say no?'], ['gus', 'You will not say no. Come down. See it.']]\n  ],\n  gusReturn: [['gus', 'I am a patient man. But even I have a calendar.'], ['gus', 'Bring me the product, Mr. Whitewash. Not excuses.']],\n  gusPaid: [['gus', 'Impeccable. As promised. The rest is in the envelope. Please, take some chicken.']],\n  gusNoStuff: [['gus', 'You do not have what I asked for. We will not discuss anything else.']],\n  hank: [['hank', 'Walter! Hey! Haha. You look like a guy who has not slept. Are you okay? Skyler says you have been cooking late. At the car wash? Seriously?'],\n         ['walt', 'I have a lot on my plate, Hank.'], ['hank', 'We should have the boys over. Barbecue. I will bring the Schrader. I mean the, uh, Schrodinger. Still working on the name.']],\n  hatch: [['gus', '(Through the intercom) Come down, Mr. Whitewash. The door is open.'], ['walt', 'This is it. Down the ladder, into the hole in the ground.']],\n  hatchShut: [['walt', 'The hatch is welded shut. Whatever is down there, I am not ready for it. Not yet. Not until the money is in the bank, or the calendar runs out.']],\n  bossIntro: [\n    ['gus', 'You cook very well, Mr. Whitewash. But this is a business. And a business does not tolerate a man who thinks he is the owner.'],\n    ['walt', 'I am not the owner. I am the one who knocks.'],\n    ['gus', 'Then knock.']],\n  bossHalf: [['gus', 'You are making this unnecessarily untidy.'], ['walt', 'Say my name.']],\n  bossDown: [['gus', 'Do you know what it costs, to be a man like me?'], ['walt', 'I am not in danger, Gus. I am the danger.']],\n  endWin: [\n    ['narrator', 'The Superlab went quiet. Somewhere above, in the desert, a rattlesnake crossed the road and nobody stopped to watch.'],\n    ['walt', 'I did it. I did all of it. And I did it for the family.'],\n    ['narrator', 'That is what he told himself.']],\n  endLate: [['narrator', 'Day Five ended. The clock ran out before the Superlab did. Albuquerky does not wait for a cough.']],\n  bust: [['cop', 'Sir, step away from the RV. We have received a number of calls about a smell.'], ['walt', 'It is a chemistry experiment.'], ['cop', 'That is what they all say.']],\n  customerBuy: [['customer', 'Yo. You the guy? The blue guy? I heard about you. I need one.']],\n  customerNo: [['customer', 'You got nothin\\'? Come on, man. Do not waste my time.']],\n  customerHappy: [['customer', 'Oh man. Oh MAN. That is beautiful.']],\n  noMoney: [['walt', 'I cannot afford that.']],\n  needBricks: [['walt', 'I have nothing to sell. The bricks are the product. The product is the bricks.']],\n  noIngredients: [['walt', 'No ingredients. I need a batch from the supply store before Jimmy and I can cook.']],\n  tooLate: [['walt', 'It is too dark to cook. Even I need sleep. Home. Bed.']],\n  tutorial: [\n    ['Move', 'Left stick or WASD. Walk to the glowing markers. Press the interact button on any marker to use it.'],\n    ['The loop', 'Buy ingredients at the supply store, cook at the RV, sell to the corner customers, launder at the car wash.'],\n    ['Heat', 'Cops notice you when the heat is high or you do anything loud. Break their line of sight to cool off.'],\n    ['Fight', 'Square / J / click hits. Hold aim and shoot with the pistol. Triangle / Q switches weapon.']\n  ]\n};\n\n// the day summary and the one-liners at day's end\nW.dayLines = ['A day like any other, which is the problem.', 'The numbers are moving. So is the cough.', 'Everybody has a limit. Yours has not arrived yet.', 'Four days in. You do not recognise the man in the mirror.', 'Tomorrow is the last day.'];\n\nWW.world = W;\nif (typeof module !== 'undefined') module.exports = W;\n})();\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014tzCVeXJ4fH9Gpj5qbR3wT","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-183711__xb81546/work/Walter-Whitewash-BreakingBad-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261102-183711/src/10-world.js (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8704baa7-6f68-414d-afec-f55fd2d8121c","uuid":"7fe4ef3f-56d0-4a50-8d16-1725a9d75075","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:42:29.651Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-183711__xb81546/work/Walter-Whitewash-BreakingBad-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261102-183711/src/10-world.js","content":"// WALTER WHITEWASH: the places. Two maps built from code: Albuquerky (the town, the desert, the car wash, the RV) and the\n// Superlab (the last room). Also the people's looks and every line anyone says. Pure data, plus builders that need the engine.\n(() => {\nconst WW = (globalThis.WW = globalThis.WW || {});\nconst W = {};\n\n// ---- the town -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 48 x 34 cells of 16 units. '.' sand, 'r' road, 'p' sidewalk, 'w' wet concrete (car wash), '#' rim rocks. Buildings are\n// wall types: 1 house, 2 school, 3 rim rock, 4 RV, 5 car wash, 6 supply store, 7 Los Polluelos, 8 fence\nW.COLS = 48; W.ROWS = 34;\nW.townRows = () => {\n  const g = Array.from({ length: W.ROWS }, () => Array(W.COLS).fill('.'));\n  const fill = (x0, y0, x1, y1, ch) => { for (let y = y0; y <= y1; y++) for (let x = x0; x <= x1; x++) g[y][x] = ch; };\n  const put = (x, y, ch) => { g[y][x] = ch; };\n  // roads and sidewalks\n  fill(1, 13, 46, 17, 'p'); fill(1, 14, 46, 16, 'r'); fill(21, 1, 25, 32, 'p'); fill(22, 1, 24, 32, 'r'); fill(21, 13, 25, 17, 'p'); fill(22, 13, 24, 17, 'r');\n  fill(1, 14, 46, 16, 'r');\n  // sidewalks in front of the buildings\n  fill(2, 10, 15, 10, 'p'); fill(28, 10, 36, 10, 'p'); fill(38, 10, 46, 10, 'p'); fill(28, 27, 38, 27, 'p');\n  // buildings\n  fill(2, 2, 15, 9, '2'); fill(28, 2, 36, 8, '1'); fill(37, 2, 46, 9, '7'); fill(28, 19, 38, 26, '6');\n  fill(40, 21, 46, 24, '4');\n  // car wash: three walls, open to the south, wet floor, a counter spot\n  fill(2, 19, 14, 27, 'w'); fill(2, 19, 14, 19, '5'); fill(2, 19, 2, 27, '5'); fill(14, 19, 14, 27, '5');\n  fill(5, 19, 6, 20, '5');\n  // two bays divided by short walls, cars sit between them\n  fill(7, 24, 7, 26, '5'); fill(10, 24, 10, 26, '5');\n  // the rim\n  for (let x = 0; x < W.COLS; x++) { put(x, 0, '#'); put(x, W.ROWS - 1, '#'); }\n  for (let y = 0; y < W.ROWS; y++) { put(0, y, '#'); put(W.COLS - 1, y, '#'); }\n  // gaps for the roads through the rim stay closed: it is a closed town (the demo's whole world)\n  // fences\n  for (let x = 17; x <= 19; x++) put(x, 22, '8');\n  for (let x = 40; x <= 44; x++) put(x, 28, '8');\n  // spawns and stations (each overwrites one cell: the cell keeps its floor)\n  const S = { '@': [32, 11], H: [32, 11], T: [9, 11], P: [42, 11], M: [33, 28], C: [43, 26], J: [41, 26], W: [8, 22], L: [43, 31], n: [19, 3], o: [45, 12], u: [12, 31],\n    D: [8, 28] };\n  for (const [ch, [x, y]] of Object.entries(S)) if (ch !== 'H') put(x, y, ch);\n  const X = [[5, 12], [17, 12], [27, 12], [20, 29], [36, 12], [44, 18], [6, 31], [30, 31], [18, 18], [26, 18]];\n  for (const [x, y] of X) put(x, y, 'x');\n  const E = [[30, 31], [44, 30], [36, 30], [12, 30], [5, 17], [18, 25], [34, 17], [45, 19], [27, 29]];\n  for (const [x, y] of E) put(x, y, 'e');\n  for (const [x, y] of [[22, 2], [22, 31], [2, 15]]) put(x, y, 'c');\n  return g.map(r => r.join(''));\n};\nW.townLegend = {\n  '.': { floor: 'sand' }, r: { floor: 'road' }, p: { floor: 'walk' }, w: { floor: 'wet' },\n  '#': 3, 1: 1, 2: 2, 4: 4, 5: 5, 6: 6, 7: 7, 8: 8,\n  '@': { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'hero' }, T: { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'teacher' }, P: { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'gus' }, M: { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'shop' },\n  C: { floor: 'sand', spawn: 'cook' }, J: { floor: 'sand', spawn: 'jimmy' }, W: { floor: 'wet', spawn: 'counter' }, L: { floor: 'sand', spawn: 'hatch' },\n  n: { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'drop-north' }, o: { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'drop-east' }, u: { floor: 'sand', spawn: 'drop-south' }, D: { floor: 'wet', spawn: 'sol' },\n  x: { floor: 'walk', spawn: 'customer' }, e: { floor: 'sand', spawn: 'thug' }, c: { floor: 'road', spawn: 'cop' }\n};\nW.townTypes = {\n  1: { h: 34, top: '#a86a4a', side: '#d9b48a', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles' },\n  2: { h: 38, top: '#8a5a4a', side: '#a2573d', face: 'brick', roof: 'slab' },\n  3: { h: 26, top: '#8a6a4a', side: '#a07a52', face: 'rock', roof: 'plain' },\n  4: { h: 28, top: '#e8ecee', side: '#d4dadc', face: 'plain', roof: 'plain', line: '#4a9aa8' },\n  5: { h: 26, top: '#5fa0c8', side: '#c8dce8', face: 'plaster', roof: 'plain' },\n  6: { h: 32, top: '#6a6a72', side: '#c4a45a', face: 'plank', roof: 'slab' },\n  7: { h: 36, top: '#b8362a', side: '#f0c030', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles' },\n  8: { h: 9, top: '#8a6a4a', side: '#7a5a3a', face: 'plank', roof: 'plain' }\n};\nW.townFloor = (x, y, tag) => {\n  const E = My3D2dge, n = E.noise2(x * .1, y * .1), n2 = E.noise2(x * .33 + 7, y * .33 + 3);\n  if (tag === 'road') {\n    const c = 36 + Math.round(n * 12) + (n2 > .78 ? 8 : 0), line = Math.abs(y % 16 - 8) < .8 && Math.floor(x / 6) % 2 === 0 && y > 224 && y < 270;\n    const vline = Math.abs(x % 16 - 8) < .8 && Math.floor(y / 6) % 2 === 0 && x > 352 && x < 400;\n    return line || vline ? [226, 190, 60] : [c, c + 2, c + 8];\n  }\n  if (tag === 'walk') { const t = (Math.floor(x / 8) + Math.floor(y / 8)) & 1, e = x % 8 < 1 || y % 8 < 1; return e ? [118, 112, 104] : t ? [168, 160, 148] : [160, 152, 140]; }\n  if (tag === 'wet') { const e = x % 16 < 1 || y % 16 < 1; const s = n2 > .8 ? 26 : 0; return e ? [70, 96, 110] : [92 + s, 138 + s, 158 + s]; }\n  if (tag === 'lab') { const e = x % 16 < 1 || y % 16 < 1; return e ? [32, 38, 44] : ((Math.floor(x / 16) + Math.floor(y / 16)) & 1) ? [72, 84, 92] : [64, 76, 84]; }\n  // sand\n  const E2 = E.tex.dirt(x, y, { base: '#c79a5e', dark: '#b3874f', light: '#d8b074' });\n  return E2;\n};\n\n// dressing: [shape, x, y, options]. Solid ones block the way. Rocks and cactus are scenery in the desert.\nW.townDress = () => {\n  const out = [];\n  const s = (id, cx, cy, o = {}) => out.push([id, cx * 16 + 8, cy * 16 + 8, o]);\n  [[30, 29], [40, 30], [8, 31], [15, 29], [34, 31], [46, 28], [3, 30], [27, 25], [39, 18], [10, 17], [4, 17]].forEach(([x, y], i) => s('rock', x, y, { params: { r: 6 + (i % 3) * 2, seed: i + 1 } }));\n  [[17, 30], [41, 29], [2, 24], [18, 19], [26, 31], [45, 28]].forEach(([x, y], i) => s('bush', x, y, { params: { r: 6 + (i % 2) * 2 } }));\n  s('barrel', 30, 27, { solid: true }); s('barrel', 31, 27, { solid: true, facing: .6 }); s('crate', 37, 27, { solid: true }); s('crate', 36, 27, { solid: true, facing: .4 });\n  s('barrel', 17, 11); s('sign', 20, 12, { solid: false }); s('sack', 47 - 3, 11);\n  s('crate', 40, 20, { solid: true }); s('barrel', 41, 27, { solid: true });\n  s('cart', 5, 25, { solid: true, facing: 0 }); s('cart', 12, 25, { solid: true, facing: Math.PI }); s('barrel', 4, 21, { solid: true });\n  return out;\n};\n\n// ---- the Superlab ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nW.labRows = () => [\n  '########################',\n  '#......................#',\n  '#..#..................#.#',\n  '#..#....G.............#.#',\n  '#......................#.#',\n  '#....#..........#......#',\n  '#...............#......#',\n  '#.......tt.............#',\n  '#.......tt.............#',\n  '#....#..........#......#',\n  '#......................#',\n  '#..#..................#.#',\n  '#..#......@...........#.#',\n  '#......................#',\n  '########################'];\nW.labLegend = { '.': { floor: 'lab' }, '#': 1, t: { floor: 'lab', tile: 2 }, G: { floor: 'lab', spawn: 'boss' }, '@': { floor: 'lab', spawn: 'hero' } };\nW.labTypes = {\n  1: { h: 40, top: '#4a5560', side: '#6a7884', face: 'plain', roof: 'plain', line: '#2a3238' },\n  2: { h: 20, top: '#8ab8d8', side: '#5a8aa8', face: 'plain', roof: 'plain' }\n};\n\n// ---- people --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// each is a Humanoid spec. Walt wears the green shirt and the khaki; in the cook he is in the yellow suit.\nW.looks = {\n  walt:   { size: 1.2, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'bald', hat: { style: 'cap', color: '#2a2a2a' }, colors: { skin: '#e8c8b0', cloth: '#8a9a5a', pants: '#b8a070', boot: '#4a3a2a', hair: '#3a2a20' } },\n  waltgun:{ size: 1.2, build: 'chibi', weapon: 'gun', outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'bald', hat: { style: 'cap', color: '#2a2a2a' }, colors: { skin: '#e8c8b0', cloth: '#8a9a5a', pants: '#b8a070', boot: '#4a3a2a', metal: '#3a3a42' } },\n  hazmat: { size: 1.2, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'bald', hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#d8c020' }, colors: { skin: '#e8c8b0', cloth: '#e0c828', coat: '#e0c828', pants: '#d8c020', boot: '#2a2a2a', glove: '#2a2a2a' } },\n  jimmy:  { size: 1.15, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'short', hair: 'short', hat: { style: 'cap', color: '#d8d8d8' }, colors: { skin: '#e0b898', cloth: '#6a6ae0', pants: '#3a4a6a', hair: '#8a6a3a', boot: '#d8d8d8' } },\n  gus:    { size: 1.35, build: 'heroic', weapon: 'gun', outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'short', colors: { skin: '#d8b090', cloth: '#d8c8a8', coat: '#a8b4b8', pants: '#5a5a62', hair: '#6a5a4a', boot: '#2a2a2a', metal: '#2a2a32' } },\n  cop:    { size: 1.2, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'short', hair: 'short', hat: { style: 'cap', color: '#1a2a5a' }, colors: { skin: '#e0b898', cloth: '#3a5a98', pants: '#1a2a4a', boot: '#1a1a1a', hair: '#2a2a2a' } },\n  hank:   { size: 1.3, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'short', hair: 'short', colors: { skin: '#d8b090', cloth: '#d8d4c8', pants: '#3a3a3a', boot: '#1a1a1a', hair: '#2a2018' } },\n  thug:   { size: 1.2, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'none', hair: 'spiky', colors: { skin: '#b88a68', cloth: '#a8281c', pants: '#2a2a3a', boot: '#1a1a1a', hair: '#1a1a1a' } },\n  shooter:{ size: 1.2, build: 'chibi', weapon: 'gun', outfit: 'shirt', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'ponytail', hat: { style: 'band', color: '#d8d8d8' }, colors: { skin: '#a87a58', cloth: '#6a1a8a', pants: '#2a2a3a', boot: '#1a1a1a', hair: '#1a1a1a' } },\n  enforcer:{ size: 1.45, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'bald', colors: { skin: '#a87a58', cloth: '#d8b020', coat: '#2a2a32', pants: '#1a1a1a', boot: '#0a0a0a' } },\n  teacher:{ size: 1.15, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'robe', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'long', colors: { skin: '#d8a888', cloth: '#9a4a7a', hair: '#4a2a2a' } },\n  sol:    { size: 1.15, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'short', colors: { skin: '#d8b090', cloth: '#d86a98', coat: '#e8e0c8', pants: '#3a2a4a', hair: '#3a2a20' } }\n};\nW.customerLook = i => {\n  const hairs = ['short', 'long', 'spiky', 'ponytail', 'bald'], cl = ['#c85a5a', '#5a8ac8', '#7ab85a', '#c8a85a', '#8a5ac8', '#5ac8b8', '#a0a0a8'], sk = ['#f0d0b8', '#d8a888', '#a87a58', '#7a5238', '#e8c8a8'];\n  return { size: 1.1, build: 'chibi', weapon: null, outfit: i % 3 === 0 ? 'robe' : 'shirt', sleeves: i % 2 ? 'long' : 'short', hair: hairs[i % hairs.length],\n    colors: { skin: sk[i % sk.length], cloth: cl[(i * 3) % cl.length], pants: '#4a4a5a', boot: '#2a2a2a', hair: ['#2a1a10', '#6a4a20', '#1a1a1a', '#a08a50'][i % 4] } };\n};\n\n// ---- the words ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Voices are gibberish (the game babbles each speaker at their own pitch), so the text carries it: dry, short, mean to itself.\nW.pitch = { walt: 150, jimmy: 260, gus: 120, cop: 200, hank: 135, thug: 170, teacher: 300, sol: 230, customer: 240, narrator: 190, enforcer: 95 };\nW.names = { walt: 'WALT', jimmy: 'JIMMY', gus: 'GUS FRYING', cop: 'OFFICER', hank: 'HANK SCHRODINGER', thug: 'THUG', teacher: 'MS. CHALKWELL', sol: 'SOL GOODGIRL', customer: 'CUSTOMER', narrator: '', enforcer: 'ENFORCER' };\n\nW.script = {\n  intro: [\n    ['narrator', 'Albuquerky, New Mexico. A Tuesday that looked like all the others.'],\n    ['walt', 'Fifty-two years old. Sixteen years teaching chemistry to kids who would rather be asleep. A second job at a car wash, wiping down other people\\'s Hondas.'],\n    ['walt', 'And now the doctor says I have a cough that is not a cough. The bills are $600 a day, and they do not care that I am a nice man.'],\n    ['walt', 'I know chemistry. Better than anyone in this state. It is time to put it to work.'],\n    ['walt', 'Eighteen thousand dollars, clean, in five days. That is the number. Cook, sell, launder. And be home for dinner.']\n  ],\n  teacher: [\n    ['teacher', 'Walter! You are in early. The students will be so excited to see you. Okay, no, that was a lie. But I am glad you are here.'],\n    ['walt', 'I am only passing by, Ms. Chalkwell. I forgot my pens.'],\n    ['teacher', 'You look tired. Have you been to see anyone?'],\n    ['walt', 'I have been to see everyone.']\n  ],\n  jimmyFirst: [\n    ['jimmy', 'Yo, Mr. White-wash! You came! I knew it, I told everyone, I said Mr. Whitewash is gonna cook. Bro, this RV is so sick.'],\n    ['walt', 'Jimmy. Never say my name out loud. And it is not \"sick.\" It is a mobile laboratory with a leak in the roof.'],\n    ['jimmy', 'Okay, okay. So, you buy the stuff at the supply store, bring it here, and we cook. I handle the, uh, vibes.'],\n    ['walt', 'You handle the vibes. Fine. Measure, heat, filter. We do this the right way, or we do not do this.']\n  ],\n  jimmyNoStuff: [\n    ['jimmy', 'Yo. Uh. We need ingredients first. Supply store, down the road. Eight hundred a batch. Bring it and I will be here, being supportive.']\n  ],\n  jimmyTips: [\n    [['jimmy', 'Sell it to the corner guys. Anybody with a dollar sign over their head. Do not do it in front of a cop. Pretty sure that is in the rules.']],\n    [['jimmy', 'The car wash takes a quarter. A quarter! Sol says it is a \"very reasonable laundering coefficient.\" Whatever that means.']],\n    [['jimmy', 'Better purity, better price. Ninety-nine percent is blue. Blue is, like, a brand. You are a brand, Mr. White-wash.']],\n    [['jimmy', 'Rivals hang out in the desert. If they come at you, hit them with your wrench. Or the pistol. I would pick the pistol.']]\n  ],\n  solFirst: [\n    ['sol', 'Walter Whitewash! The man, the myth, the cough. Sol Goodgirl, attorney at car wash. Do you have a minute? Or, more importantly, do you have a minimum?'],\n    ['walt', 'I have a lot of money that is not exactly mine, and a need for it to become mine.'],\n    ['sol', 'Beautiful. Hand it to me in the bay, I will say it was a very busy week for hot wax. I keep a quarter. The government keeps the rest of its questions.'],\n    ['sol', 'Two grand a day through the front bays. We add bays, we add grand. It is a growth industry.']\n  ],\n  solWelcome: [['sol', 'Welcome back to the Whitewash Auto Spa. Where everything comes out clean. Everything.']],\n  gus: [\n    [['gus', 'Mr. Whitewash. Sit. Eat. The chicken is excellent. Everything I do is excellent.'],\n     ['gus', 'I have heard of your product. They say it is blue. I do not believe it. Prove it. Three bricks at seventy percent, by the east gate.'],\n     ['walt', 'And if I do?'], ['gus', 'Then we will talk about what it is you want. Everyone wants something.']],\n    [['gus', 'Mr. Whitewash. Good. You are punctual. I respect that.'],\n     ['gus', 'My organization has a problem. A rival crew from the desert is cutting into my corners. They are loud. I do not like loud.'],\n     ['walt', 'And you want me to handle it?'], ['gus', 'I want you to cook. The crew will handle itself, in time.']],\n    [['gus', 'You have a visitor. A DEA agent named Schrodinger has been parked outside the restaurant. He is on the phone with his wife. It is... touching.'],\n     ['walt', 'Hank is my brother-in-law.'], ['gus', 'Then be careful at the dinner table. His coffee is better than his instincts.']],\n    [['gus', 'Four days. You have the numbers, I have mine. Between us we could own this city.'],\n     ['walt', 'I am not interested in owning a city. I am interested in paying for a hospital.'], ['gus', 'Of course. That is what everyone says. Then the money starts to taste good.']],\n    [['gus', 'It is the last day. I think you know what comes next. I have a laboratory under the desert. A hundred and fifty thousand dollars a day. It is yours, if you come to work for me.'],\n     ['walt', 'And if I say no?'], ['gus', 'You will not say no. Come down. See it.']]\n  ],\n  gusReturn: [['gus', 'I am a patient man. But even I have a calendar.'], ['gus', 'Bring me the product, Mr. Whitewash. Not excuses.']],\n  gusPaid: [['gus', 'Impeccable. As promised. The rest is in the envelope. Please, take some chicken.']],\n  gusNoStuff: [['gus', 'You do not have what I asked for. We will not discuss anything else.']],\n  hank: [['hank', 'Walter! Hey! Haha. You look like a guy who has not slept. Are you okay? Skyler says you have been cooking late. At the car wash? Seriously?'],\n         ['walt', 'I have a lot on my plate, Hank.'], ['hank', 'We should have the boys over. Barbecue. I will bring the Schrader. I mean the, uh, Schrodinger. Still working on the name.']],\n  hatch: [['gus', '(Through the intercom) Come down, Mr. Whitewash. The door is open.'], ['walt', 'This is it. Down the ladder, into the hole in the ground.']],\n  hatchShut: [['walt', 'The hatch is welded shut. Whatever is down there, I am not ready for it. Not yet. Not until the money is in the bank, or the calendar runs out.']],\n  bossIntro: [\n    ['gus', 'You cook very well, Mr. Whitewash. But this is a business. And a business does not tolerate a man who thinks he is the owner.'],\n    ['walt', 'I am not the owner. I am the one who knocks.'],\n    ['gus', 'Then knock.']],\n  bossHalf: [['gus', 'You are making this unnecessarily untidy.'], ['walt', 'Say my name.']],\n  bossDown: [['gus', 'Do you know what it costs, to be a man like me?'], ['walt', 'I am not in danger, Gus. I am the danger.']],\n  endWin: [\n    ['narrator', 'The Superlab went quiet. Somewhere above, in the desert, a rattlesnake crossed the road and nobody stopped to watch.'],\n    ['walt', 'I did it. I did all of it. And I did it for the family.'],\n    ['narrator', 'That is what he told himself.']],\n  endLate: [['narrator', 'Day Five ended. The clock ran out before the Superlab did. Albuquerky does not wait for a cough.']],\n  bust: [['cop', 'Sir, step away from the RV. We have received a number of calls about a smell.'], ['walt', 'It is a chemistry experiment.'], ['cop', 'That is what they all say.']],\n  customerBuy: [['customer', 'Yo. You the guy? The blue guy? I heard about you. I need one.']],\n  customerNo: [['customer', 'You got nothin\\'? Come on, man. Do not waste my time.']],\n  customerHappy: [['customer', 'Oh man. Oh MAN. That is beautiful.']],\n  noMoney: [['walt', 'I cannot afford that.']],\n  needBricks: [['walt', 'I have nothing to sell. The bricks are the product. The product is the bricks.']],\n  noIngredients: [['walt', 'No ingredients. I need a batch from the supply store before Jimmy and I can cook.']],\n  tooLate: [['walt', 'It is too dark to cook. Even I need sleep. Home. Bed.']],\n  tutorial: [\n    ['Move', 'Left stick or WASD. Walk to the glowing markers. Press the interact button on any marker to use it.'],\n    ['The loop', 'Buy ingredients at the supply store, cook at the RV, sell to the corner customers, launder at the car wash.'],\n    ['Heat', 'Cops notice you when the heat is high or you do anything loud. Break their line of sight to cool off.'],\n    ['Fight', 'Square / J / click hits. Hold aim and shoot with the pistol. Triangle / Q switches weapon.']\n  ]\n};\n\n// the day summary and the one-liners at day's end\nW.dayLines = ['A day like any other, which is the problem.', 'The numbers are moving. So is the cough.', 'Everybody has a limit. Yours has not arrived yet.', 'Four days in. You do not recognise the man in the mirror.', 'Tomorrow is the last day.'];\n\nWW.world = W;\nif (typeof module !== 'undefined') module.exports = W;\n})();\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014tzCVeXJ4fH9Gpj5qbR3wT","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
