hots.fire\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-300"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GVH9BF5rvqgpVwMjt6ky8Z","type":"tool_result","content":"418:- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\n419:- `r.glowDisc(g, cx, cy, rad, color, a)`: glow halo from a cache: additive light rings (alpha style) or a dithered disc (dither style). a = 0..1 strength\n420:- `r.groundArc(x, y, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha = 1, z = 0, g = this.tgt)`: a band of a ring on the ground from radius r0 to r1 and angle a0 to a1 (radians): melee telegraphs, sight cones\n421:- `r.groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a dithered disc lying on the ground (radius in world units, z its height): shadows, auras, area attacks\n423:- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\n424:- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040', offscreen: 'arrow' }\n425:- `r.overlay(fn)`: draw fn(g) on top of everything, in screen pixels (HUD, dialog, menus)\n427:- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also adds a warm light to game.lights. A prop at least chest high (E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22: a pillar, a stat\n429:- `r.shadow(x, y, rad, alpha = .5, color = '#0c0818', z = 0)`: soft contact shadow under a character: a cached dithered ellipse, correct for the current view. z = height of the surface it falls on (0 = floor; the top of a block or platform otherwise)\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', alpha: .3, rays }. Call it \n435:- `r.text(str, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o)`: HUD text in screen pixels, drawn on top and never lit: r.text('SCORE 120', 4, 4, '#fff', { align, scale, outline })\n436:- `r.textAt(x, y, z, str, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: text floating at a world point (names, prompts): r.textAt(x, y, z, 'OPEN', '#ffe08a')\n669:- `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size = 40, o = {})` †: a close-up bust for dialog boxes and menus, drawn live from the rig (blinks, hair and hats included): rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 40, { zoom: 3, turn: .6, bg: '#1a2050', frame: true }) // inside r.overlay(g => ...) zoom: pixels per world unit (3 = face fills the frame), turn:\n1089:- `E.PROPS: torch, candle, candelabra, chandelier, brazier, window, banner, pillar, statue, crate, barrel, chest, pot, sign, fence, lamp, door, tree, pine, bush, flowers, grass, rock, crystal, bones, skull, vines, cobweb, lantern, streetlamp, awning, hydrant, trashcan, firedrum, sandbags, cactus, palm, mushroom` †: the name\n1155:- `E.ui`: pixel-drawn interface pieces for r.overlay\n20:- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n73:- 815 Flow field; E.FlowField: flow\n817:- `new E.FlowField(map, o = {}) → flow`: new E.FlowField(map, { step: 2, climb: 0, drop: 0, jump: 0 }): distances over the tops a body can stand on (E.HEIGHTS). With no options it covers the floor (and walls no higher than step, which bodies walk over); a target on a roof gets a field across the\n818:- `new E.FlowField({ step, climb, drop })`: next-door cells connect when their tops differ by at most step, or going up by up to climb and down by up to drop (agents that climb walls or hop down)\n819:- `new E.FlowField({ jump })`: (world units) links tops across a gap that a jump clears, straight along a row or column, by map.landing's rules (up to jumpRise higher, 11, and jumpDrop lower, 18): an agent with E.Mover's leap chases across roofs. With jump, distances are travel: a jump of k cell\n820:- `flow.dir(x, y, fx, fy)`: normalized ground direction to walk from (x, y) toward the target (straight at it where the field doesn't reach)\n69:- 638 Humanoid rig; E.Attack: slash, E.Combo: combo, E.Humanoid: rig\n653:- `new E.Combo(specs, o = {}) → combo`: new E.Combo(items, { window: .3 }): items are move names, specs or Attacks\n658:- `combo.hits(targets, test, fn)`: the current hit's hits(targets, test, fn): fn(target) once per swing where test(target) is true\n703:- `E.MOVES: slash, backslash, overhead, rising, thrust, spin, plunge, twohand, jab, cross, hook, uppercut, haymaker, elbow, ... (24)`: a library of named attacks with timing and body motion (anticipation, lunge, step, twist, hop). new E.Attack('overhead'),\n1564:- `rhythm.maxCombo = 0` †: the longest combo\n1023:- `shots.fire(b)`: fire one bullet. Fields: x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, r, dmg, life, team, color, core, sprite, pierce, grav, data\n1024:- `shots.hit(targets, fn, team)`: test bullets of `team` against targets (objects with x, y, z and r, or w/h in side view). fn(bullet, target). Returns hits","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8704baa7-6f68-414d-afec-f55fd2d8121c","uuid":"b44a8451-104d-4bff-85e0-9f80c255c934","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:48:20.361Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"418:- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\n419:- `r.glowDisc(g, cx, cy, rad, color, a)`: glow halo from a cache: additive light rings (alpha style) or a dithered disc (dither style). a = 0..1 strength\n420:- `r.groundArc(x, y, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha = 1, z = 0, g = this.tgt)`: a band of a ring on the ground from radius r0 to r1 and angle a0 to a1 (radians): melee telegraphs, sight cones\n421:- `r.groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a dithered disc lying on the ground (radius in world units, z its height): shadows, auras, area attacks\n423:- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\n424:- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040', offscreen: 'arrow' }\n425:- `r.overlay(fn)`: draw fn(g) on top of everything, in screen pixels (HUD, dialog, menus)\n427:- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also adds a warm light to game.lights. A prop at least chest high (E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22: a pillar, a stat\n429:- `r.shadow(x, y, rad, alpha = .5, color = '#0c0818', z = 0)`: soft contact shadow under a character: a cached dithered ellipse, correct for the current view. z = height of the surface it falls on (0 = floor; the top of a block or platform otherwise)\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', alpha: .3, rays }. Call it \n435:- `r.text(str, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o)`: HUD text in screen pixels, drawn on top and never lit: r.text('SCORE 120', 4, 4, '#fff', { align, scale, outline })\n436:- `r.textAt(x, y, z, str, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: text floating at a world point (names, prompts): r.textAt(x, y, z, 'OPEN', '#ffe08a')\n669:- `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size = 40, o = {})` †: a close-up bust for dialog boxes and menus, drawn live from the rig (blinks, hair and hats included): rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 40, { zoom: 3, turn: .6, bg: '#1a2050', frame: true }) // inside r.overlay(g => ...) zoom: pixels per world unit (3 = face fills the frame), turn:\n1089:- `E.PROPS: torch, candle, candelabra, chandelier, brazier, window, banner, pillar, statue, crate, barrel, chest, pot, sign, fence, lamp, door, tree, pine, bush, flowers, grass, rock, crystal, bones, skull, vines, cobweb, lantern, streetlamp, awning, hydrant, trashcan, firedrum, sandbags, cactus, palm, mushroom` †: the name\n1155:- `E.ui`: pixel-drawn interface pieces for r.overlay\n20:- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n73:- 815 Flow field; E.FlowField: flow\n817:- `new E.FlowField(map, o = {}) → flow`: new E.FlowField(map, { step: 2, climb: 0, drop: 0, jump: 0 }): distances over the tops a body can stand on (E.HEIGHTS). With no options it covers the floor (and walls no higher than step, which bodies walk over); a target on a roof gets a field across the\n818:- `new E.FlowField({ step, climb, drop })`: next-door cells connect when their tops differ by at most step, or going up by up to climb and down by up to drop (agents that climb walls or hop down)\n819:- `new E.FlowField({ jump })`: (world units) links tops across a gap that a jump clears, straight along a row or column, by map.landing's rules (up to jumpRise higher, 11, and jumpDrop lower, 18): an agent with E.Mover's leap chases across roofs. With jump, distances are travel: a jump of k cell\n820:- `flow.dir(x, y, fx, fy)`: normalized ground direction to walk from (x, y) toward the target (straight at it where the field doesn't reach)\n69:- 638 Humanoid rig; E.Attack: slash, E.Combo: combo, E.Humanoid: rig\n653:- `new E.Combo(specs, o = {}) → combo`: new E.Combo(items, { window: .3 }): items are move names, specs or Attacks\n658:- `combo.hits(targets, test, fn)`: the current hit's hits(targets, test, fn): fn(target) once per swing where test(target) is true\n703:- `E.MOVES: slash, backslash, overhead, rising, thrust, spin, plunge, twohand, jab, cross, hook, uppercut, haymaker, elbow, ... (24)`: a library of named attacks with timing and body motion (anticipation, lunge, step, twist, hop). new E.Attack('overhead'),\n1564:- `rhythm.maxCombo = 0` †: the longest combo\n1023:- `shots.fire(b)`: fire one bullet. Fields: x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, r, dmg, life, team, color, core, sprite, pierce, grav, data\n1024:- `shots.hit(targets, fn, team)`: test bullets of `team` against targets (objects with x, y, z and r, or w/h in side view). fn(bullet, target). Returns hits","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GVH9BF5rvqgpVwMjt6ky8Z","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
