behaviour, and the Done list. Each could be tested, and a random title choice by code is a nice touch.\",\n    \"How big the scope is next to 'a vertical slice of a game engine': feature-complete and polished demo, plus multiplayer, plus attract mode, plus a full test pass. It was also not clear if a hub round should replace the title and story, or if both are needed (I kept both). Typos such as 'woudl' in the feedback questions.\",\n    \"Balancing an economy and a boss fight without a human playtest, and keeping every system working with every other at once: the bugs lived in the seams, not in the parts.\",\n    \"A person playing on a TV with a real DualSense from 10 feet: whether text sizes, prompts, stick feel and the dodge timing are right. A bot can prove the game is finishable but not that it feels good.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Walter Whitewash\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Cook. Sell. Launder. Don't get caught.\",\n    \"description\": \"A chemistry teacher with a cough and a bill cooks blue product, sells it to the corner, launders it at a car wash and dodges the cops, then goes down to the Superlab to face Gus Frying. A parody spiritual successor to Breaking Bad.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Action\",\n    \"source\": \"Breaking Bad (2008-2013)\",\n    \"series\": \"Breaking Bad\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Move: left stick or WASD · aim: right stick or mouse · interact: Cross or E · attack: Square or J or click · dodge: Circle or Space · switch weapon: Triangle or Q · sprint: R1 or Shift · pills: L1 or H\",\n    \"tags\": [\"top-down\", \"pixel art\", \"story\", \"stealth\", \"boss fights\", \"comedy\"]\n  }\n}\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GCLrqjkBLHE7PYW4VcVkPq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
